    "This gives access to all public classes and methods within this module. The most straightforward way to produce the analogue sample is to use the `AnalogueSample` class. It expects parameters: `base_path` that determines the path to the Illustris data, `selection_config` that determines how the initial subhalo sample is generated, and `selection_config` that determines how the analogue sample is generated by filters. Additionally, it has optional parameters: `verbose` that prints diagnostics of the analogue generation process if True (default), and `snap` for the snapshot to use for samples (default is 99)."
   ]
